;; One integer per named set in `.agents/reading-sets.edn`: the highest
;; value that set's `:budget-lines` is allowed to take.
;; `ehrt.docs-tooling.reading-set-budget-test` fails the build on any
;; budget above its entry here, with the message "compact, or bump by
;; compaction ADR -- never in a build session". A budget may always
;; fall below its baseline; compaction is never gated.
;;
;; Why this file exists. The budget test was a ceiling that moved
;; whenever it was hit. Its own file records the history without
;; flinching: fourteen in-place bumps through 2026-08-05, superseded by
;; one re-baseline, then eleven more dated re-derivations through
;; 2026-08-16 -- twenty-five upward moves, every one of them honest and
;; individually justified, which is exactly why none of them was ever
;; the moment someone stopped and compacted instead. A gate a session
;; can satisfy by editing the gate is a measurement, not a limit.
;;
;; This file is edited ONLY by a compaction ADR, which sets each value
;; from that ADR's own post-compaction measured actual times 1.15,
;; rounded up to the nearest 5 (the standing formula, defined in
;; `.agents/reading-sets.edn`'s own header). A build session that finds
;; itself wanting to edit this file has found its STOP-AND-REPORT.
